# Redis: Streaming Platform Real-Time Operations
# Handles high-velocity session data, bookmarks, and trending lists.

# 1. User Session Management (Hash)
# Triggered when a user logs in or opens the app.
HSET session:user:1001 user_id "1001" device "SmartTV_LivingRoom" ip "192.168.1.50" login_time "1717200000"
EXPIRE session:user:1001 3600

# 2. Continue Watching (Bookmark)
# Stores the playback position in seconds for specific content.
# Key: bookmark:user:{user_id}:content:{content_id}
SET bookmark:user:1001:content:mv_88392 1245
# Expire bookmarks after 30 days if not active
EXPIRE bookmark:user:1001:content:mv_88392 2592000

# 3. Trending Leaderboard (Sorted Set)
# Increment score when a movie is played.
# Key: trending:movies:daily
ZINCRBY trending:movies:daily 1 "mv_88392"
ZINCRBY trending:movies:daily 1 "mv_99100"

# Get Top 3 Trending Movies
ZREVRANGE trending:movies:daily 0 2 WITHSCORES

# 4. User Profile Cache (JSON - Orbit RedisJSON Compat)
# Storing user preferences for quick personalization.
JSON.SET user:profile:1001 $ '{"id": 1001, "preferences": {"genres": ["Sci-Fi", "Action"], "autoplay": true}, "subscription": "Premium_4K"}'

# Update autoplay setting
JSON.SET user:profile:1001 $.preferences.autoplay false

# Retrieve user subscription tier
JSON.GET user:profile:1001 $.subscription

# 5. Rate Limiting (Streams/Concurrency)
# Prevent account sharing abuse (allow max 3 concurrent streams).
# Increment active streams counter
INCR streams:user:1001
# (Application logic checks if value > 3 then denies)
# On stream end:
DECR streams:user:1001
